content.text:
Now write game.js. This is the big task. Let me draft carefully.

I'll write the whole file with clear sections. Need to avoid unsupported APIs in three r160 (fine).

Potential issues:
- `THREE.SRGBColorSpace` exists.
- `renderer.toneMapping = THREE.ACESFilmicToneMapping` exists.
- `CylinderGeometry`.
- Shape/Extrude for star.
- `SpriteMaterial({map, depthTest:false, transparent:true})`.
- Text canvas.

Let's draft.

```js
import * as THREE from './vendor/three.module.min.js';

/* DOM */
const $ = ...
const ui = {...}

/* constants */
const GROUND=462, GRAVITY=470, U=.018;
const WX = x=>(x-500)*U;
const WY = y=>(GROUND-y)*U;
const clamp=(v,a,b)=>Math.max(a,Math.min(b,v));
const lerp=(a,b,t)=>a+(b-a)*t;

/* state */
...
```

Note: `WY(462)=0`, `WY(254)=3.744`.

Renderer:
```
const renderer=new THREE.WebGLRenderer({canvas,antialias:true,alpha:false,powerPreference:'high-performance'});
renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(devicePixelRatio||1,2));
renderer.outputColorSpace=THREE.SRGBColorSpace;
renderer.toneMapping=THREE.ACESFilmicToneMapping;
renderer.toneMappingExposure=1.08;
renderer.shadowMap.enabled=true;
renderer.shadowMap.type=THREE.PCFSoftShadowMap;
```
On mobile, antialias may be heavy; okay.

Scene/fog/camera.

Camera fov set per aspect. `BASE_Z=16`.

`function resize(){}` uses `innerWidth/innerHeight`; renderer.setSize(w,h,false)? Canvas CSS is 100%. Set `renderer.setSize(w,h)` updates style too. Canvas style already. Fine.

camera aspect. Compute needed z:
```
const horizontalNeed=20.6;
const verticalNeed=11.2;
const vFov=THREE.MathUtils.degToRad(fov);
const zH=verticalNeed/2/Math.tan(vFov/2);
const zW=horizontalNeed/2/(Math.tan(vFov/2)*aspect);
CAM_Z=Math.max(15.8, zH, zW);
camera.position.set(camX,CAM_Y,CAM_Z)
```
For 1200x800 aspect1.5 fov42: zH=11.2/(0.767)=14.6, zW=20.6/(0.767*1.5)=17.9→17.9.
For 390x844 aspect .462, fov 56: tan28=.532; zH=11.2/1.064=10.5; zW=20.6/(1.064*.462)=41.9 → 41.9. Objects small. Let's instead reduce horizontalNeed to 17 on portrait? That crops x edges (sling/structures maybe at x±6.6 world, within ±8.5). Structures at WX(812)=5.6, sling -5.9. So 17 world fits all gameplay (edge ±8.5) with no margin. goal in build at 8.1! Build needs ±8.5 → 17. So use horizontalNeed = portrait ? 18 : 20.6. zW=36.6. Still far. Use fov 65 in portrait: tan32.5=.637, zW=18/(1.274*.462)=30.6. Visible height 39 world; structures 4 → 10% screen. Ground island ~ maybe. Tiny.

Alternative for portrait: rotate the game world 90°? No.

Maybe use camera with smaller distance and allow clipping of far edges; gameplay objects at ±6, need 12 world. zW at fov56, aspect .462 = 12/(1.064*.462)=24.4. Still. Structures 4/18.6 visible height = 21% of 844=177px. Actually that's okay! At z 24.4 visible height=2*.532*24.4=26 world; structure 4/26=15% = 130px. Readable. Sling and target both within 12 wide, so use horizontalNeed=13 for portrait. Build goal at 8.1 and start -5 = 13.1 wide, exactly. Good. So portrait world visible 13.4 wide, with x center 1.5 in build. Fine. Let's set portrait need=13.2. At aspect .462 fov58 (tan29=.554): zW=13.2/(1.108*.462)=25.8; zH=11.2/1.108=10.1 → 25.8. Structure 4/28.6 =14% = 118px. Acceptable.

In attack, camera target follows bird but portrait horizontal 13.4, x range ±6.7. Slingshot -5.9 and fort +4.9: fits when centered at -0.5. Use camera center -0.5 for portrait attack? If bird flies, follow. Initially cam x=-0.5 shows -7.2..6.2, fort at 5.6 fits. Good. For landscape target 0.

Define `narrow = aspect < .9`.

Camera y 5.5 z dynamic; look target y 4.2.

Now the sky texture.

Let me write makeTexture with random dots. For deterministic-ish textures, Math.random each load fine.

Grass:
```
const grassTex = makeTexture(256, (g,w,h)=>{
 g.fillStyle='#79c96a'; g.fillRect(0,0,w,h);
 for(i...){ g.fillStyle = pick greens; g.fillRect(rand,rand,1..2,3..7) }
}, 10,10);
```
Texture repeat for plane 40x30: repeat 8,6.

Wood: 128:
```
base '#cf9554'; planks rows 16px, stroke '#a76a3e' at rows, wavy grain lines, knots.
```
Stone: base '#a9b6ae', noise dots, cracks.

Water: base '#57bdd2', wavy lines '#8fe1e9'.

Sky texture background: 512x512 gradient.

Add scene.background = skyTexture. But `scene.background` with a regular texture uses screen-space, good.

Sea plane material uses water texture repeat 20,20 and offset animate.

Attack island: CylinderGeometry(11.5,12.2,1.6,64) — top radius 11.5, bottom 12.2, height 1.6, center y=-0.8. Material array: [side (dirt), top (grass), bottom]. Cylinder's groups: side, top, bottom. yes.
Top grass texture repeat? Cylinder UV top maps around; use grass material with map repeat 6. Could have weird radial. Fine.
Add a sand rim ring: `RingGeometry(10.7,11.3,64)` rotated -PI/2 at y=.01 with sandy color? Might show. Add.
Add shore rocks.

Distant: hills at z=-20, y=0. Also sea covers.

Build platforms: material array.

Now `makeTextSprite` uses depthTest false and renderOrder high. Sprite scale based on text width.

```
function makeTextSprite(text,color='#fff',bg=null,size=48){
 const pad=20; const c=document.createElement('canvas'); const g=c.getContext('2d');
 g.font=`900 ${size}px Nunito, sans-serif`; const w=Math.ceil(g.measureText(text).width)+pad*2;
 c.width=w; c.height=size*1.6;
 ...
 const tex=new CanvasTexture(c); tex.colorSpace=SRGB;
 const mat=new SpriteMaterial({map:tex,transparent:true,depthTest:false,depthWrite:false});
 const sp=new Sprite(mat); sp.scale.set(w/size*0.5, 0.8,1); // world scale
 return sp;
}
```
Hmm sprite world scale: text height 0.55 world. Width proportional. Set scale.set((w/c.height)*0.7,0.7,1). Good.

Effects float up by 0.8 world over life 1.2.

Particles: small sphere geometry shared, MeshBasicMaterial color. Create 10 meshes per burst, world positions from game coords. Velocity in world units. Add to fx group. Update each frame with gravity, fade via material.opacity. Dispose material on removal but shared? Use new material per particle color. Could pool color materials. Simpler create material per burst and share among its particles? Each fade same. Store array of {mesh, vx,vy,vz,life}. On removal, mesh.geometry shared, material dispose. Fine.

Build star burst similar.

Now model factories.

`new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial` parameters. For shared mats:
```
const M = {
 wood: new MeshStandardMaterial({map:woodTex, roughness:.85}),
 stone: new MeshStandardMaterial({map:stoneTex, roughness:.95}),
 grass: new MeshStandardMaterial({map:grassTex, roughness:1}),
 dirt: new MeshStandardMaterial({color:0xb78b55, roughness:1}),
 leaf: new MeshStandardMaterial({color:0x4f9f59, roughness:.9}),
 pig: ...
}
```
Textures repeat set globally; when used on different geometry sizes, repeat is same. Wood box texture may stretch but okay.

Block mesh:
```
function makeBlockMesh(b){
 const geo=new THREE.BoxGeometry(b.w*U, b.h*U, .72);
 const mat=b.material==='stone'?M.stone:M.wood;
 const mesh=new THREE.Mesh(geo,mat);
 mesh.castShadow=mesh.receiveShadow=true;
 mesh.add(edges...)
 return mesh;
}
```
Set position from data in sync.

Pig group. Unit scale then group scale. Add shadow to each child? Setting group.traverse castShadow.

Bird group scale.

Need the bird to be oriented horizontally? Model faces +X (bill). Rotation around z on launch. `group.rotation.z = -b.rotation`? b.rotation in radians. In game, rotation increases clockwise; world z rotation counterclockwise. Use mesh.rotation.z = -b.rotation.

Pig similarly.

Sling geometry create once per level? Static; create once in attackRoot. Bands need tips. We'll create `slingGroup` with bands persistent and add to attackRoot, visible mode attack. Position world. Use local coordinates: trunk from (0,0,0) to (0,.9,0), arms. Define tips local (-.34,1.42,.12) and (.22,1.3,.12). Convert with sling origin.
`const slingOrigin = new THREE.Vector3(WX(170),0,0.25);` (y0 ground).
Bands unit cylinder geometry radius .035 height1 with M.band.
`updateBand(mesh,a,b)`:
```
const dir=b.clone().sub(a); const len=dir.length();
mesh.position.copy(a).addScaledVector(dir,.5);
mesh.quaternion.setFromUnitVectors(UP,dir.normalize());
mesh.scale.set(1,len,1);
```
Unit cylinder height 1. Set radius .035.
Pouch maybe small box at anchor.

Band anchor when current bird: world (WX(bird.x), WY(bird.y), .62). When no bird, maybe hide. When launched hide. Show when !launched && currentBird.

Trajectory group: 20 meshes. Use MeshBasicMaterial white opacity .75, depthWrite false. Add to attackRoot. z=.9.

Now level data.

```
function mkBox(x,bottom,w,h,material='wood'){ return {x,y:bottom-h/2,w,h,material,hp:material==='stone'?2:1,alive:true,dynamic:false,vx:0,vy:0,spin:0,angle:0}; }
function mkPig(x,bottom,r=19){ return {x,y:bottom-r,r,alive:true,...}; }
```
For ground use bottom=GROUND.

Levels:
